Corrected message:

Fix gradient crash when changing type after undoing a gradient

Undoing a finished gradient made its handle live again, but finishing
had already released the tool's copy of the pixels from before the
gradient. Changing the gradient type or alpha blending afterwards
(with a translucent colour) re-rendered from that released copy and
crashed. The gradient now takes a fresh copy of the layer's current
content as its base when none is left.

Adds a regression test.
